<title>USA: Conrail says shareholder action lacks merit.</title>
<headline>Conrail says shareholder action lacks merit.</headline>
<dateline>PHILADELPHIA 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Conrail Inc said a group of its shareholders seeking to force CSX Corp to pay $110 cash for all of Conrail shares and to block any postponement of a December 23 shareholders meeting lacked merit in its legal action.</p>
<p>&quot;It's frivolous and without merit,&quot; the spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>The group, which is seeking to block an intended merger of CSX and Conrail and force consideration of a rival $110 per share cash offer from Norfolk Southern Corp, amended an existing federal court complaint Monday to include the new requests.</p>
</text>
